<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 19 March, from 1205 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1205">1205 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">821 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry of Flanders defeats the Nicaeans at the Battle of Adramyttion</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> crusader forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders">Henry of Flanders</a> defeated an army of the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>, led by Constantine Laskaris, at Adramyttion. Nicaea was one of the Greek states founded after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1204.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-flanders">Henry of Flanders</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1227">1227 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">799 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ugolino di Conti is elected Pope Gregory IX</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Following the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ix">Ugolino di Conti</a> was elected pope and took the name Gregory IX. He reigned until 1241 and is known for issuing the Decretales and instituting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medieval-inquisition">Papal Inquisition</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii">Pope Honorius III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1277">1277 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">749 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Byzantine Empire and Venice renew their treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> renegotiated their treaty of 1268 and extended it for two years. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII Palaiologos</a> kept the Venetian fleet out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> plans, while Venice gained wider trading privileges.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1279">1279 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">747 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongol fleet destroys the last Song forces at Yamen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a sea battle off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pearl-river">Pearl River</a> delta, Yuan forces crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> navy. The minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lu-xiufu">Lu Xiufu</a> jumped into the sea with the child emperor, completing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>'s conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1563">1563 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">463 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edict of Amboise ends the first French War of Religion</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-de-medici">Catherine de' Medici</a>'s peace allowed Huguenot nobles to worship freely and others in limited places. Neither side was satisfied, and war resumed in 1567.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1687">1687 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">339 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">René-Robert de La Salle killed by his own men</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The explorer who had claimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> basin for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> was shot by mutineers in east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> after his colony went astray. His Fort Saint Louis was soon destroyed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1859">1859 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">167 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gounod's 'Faust' premieres in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Gounod's opera, based on Goethe, opened at the Théâtre Lyrique. Revised with recitatives and a ballet, it became one of the most performed operas of the 19th century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US adopts standard time zones and daylight saving time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Standard Time Act gave legal force to time zones first used by the railways and introduced daylight saving time to save fuel. Daylight saving proved unpopular and was repealed in 1919.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler issues the 'Nero Decree'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hitler ordered the destruction of German industry, transport and supplies before they fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>. Armaments Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-speer">Albert Speer</a> worked to ensure it was largely not carried out.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 19 March <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guyuk-khan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guyuk-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Güyük Khan</span><span class="tp">1206–1248</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-anchieta"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-de-anchieta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José de Anchieta</span><span class="tp">1534–1597</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-iv-of-portugal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-iv-of-portugal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John IV of Portugal</span><span class="tp">1604–1656</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-prudencio-padilla"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-prudencio-padilla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Prudencio Padilla</span><span class="tp">1784–1828</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/david-livingstone.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">David Livingstone</span><span class="tp">1813–1873</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-francis-burton"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-francis-burton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Richard Francis Burton</span><span class="tp">1821–1890</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/zhang-zuolin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zhang-zuolin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Zhang Zuolin</span><span class="tp">1875–1928</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-speer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-speer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Speer</span><span class="tp">1905–1981</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/said-musa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/said-musa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Said Musa</span><span class="tp">b. 1944</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 19 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/severus-alexander"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/severus-alexander.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Severus Alexander</span><span class="tp">208–235</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-bearded"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-the-bearded.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry the Bearded</span><span class="tp">c. 1165–1238</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-bing-of-song"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Bing of Song</span><span class="tp">1272–1279</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alexander-iii-of-scotland"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alexander-iii-of-scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexander III of Scotland</span><span class="tp">1241–1286</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rene-robert-cavelier-sieur-de-la-salle"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rene-robert-cavelier-sieur-de-la-salle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">René-Robert Cavelier, Sieur de La Salle</span><span class="tp">1643–1687</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elias-lonnrot"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elias-lonnrot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Elias Lönnrot</span><span class="tp">1802–1884</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
